2026-09-26 — K02g: select existing bounded add/sub immediates.

RED: the MIR immediate-shape assertion and CLI assembly assertion fail, with
zero Rust compilation errors. The source's numeric result already agrees.
GREEN: full-register bits<32>/bits<64> ADD/SUB select the existing unsigned
twelve-bit immediate for directly known constants in [0,4095]. Only ADD may
commute already evaluated SSA operands. Source overflow checks, narrow/pair
paths, dynamic operands and nonmatching operations remain unchanged.

Four MIR tests: 24 selection cases, 120 exact EvoIR/MIR comparisons, eight
nonmatching/dynamic controls, two original E3004 traps and 48 Linux/Darwin
assembler encodings. The CLI case passes O0/O2 C-HIR, EvoIR, MIR and assembly.
